{
  "_doc": "Area kits (P2-010, DELHI_WORLD.md 'Area kits', KT2 and TX1): one kit per pilot archetype, each read from its area sheet and board (harness/design/areas/<area>.md and _board.jpg). `types` maps every generated building type (tools/bake/areas/schema.ts BUILDING_TYPES) to the kit that draws its modules; a module id stays `<type>.<part>` as the bake wrote it (fixed ids: a mesh is replaced by id, the placements never change). Kit fields: `area` is the names file (game/data/names/<area>.json) its sign boards take their names from; `facade` the facade colours of the kit (palette words of harness/data/areas/palette.json, the colours its profiles paint walls with: the baked tint comes from the same list); `accent` the painted parts (shutters, doors, awnings, grilles), one picked per bay; `boards` the board look (background colours, lettering, scripts in order); `shares` how often the kit adds its own pieces to a bay (sign board on a shop bay, outside stair on a blank upper bay, roof tank and roof railing on a parapet bay; residential kits carry the stair and railings, Anmol 2026-11-13); `tex` the generator parameters of the kit's tiling layers (tools/kits/make_textures.mjs).",
